@participant3 thank you for adding the documentation for the work-around!

> 2. Generate a new Rancher authentication token with the value of Scope set to No Scope. You can customize the TTL for the token (for example, a value of 0 results in tokens that do not expire).

its unclear where we should do this. Is this in the rancher instance from Harvester itself?

Thanks for the feedback, @participant9 I've opened a PR with fixes: https://github.com/harvester/harvesterhci.io/pull/69

@participant1 , could you please describe in more detail the steps you took and the errors you were seeing?

I tried to reproduce your problem as best I could with the info you gave, but in my case, the the cluster was eventually able to delete the old guest VMs.
